<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis I, Prince of Anhalt-Köthen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1579–1650</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Ludwig I of Anhalt-Köthen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis I, Prince of Anhalt-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kothen">Köthen</a> from 1603 until his death, was the first ruler of the separate principality of Anhalt-Köthen. In 1617 he founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fruitbearing-society">Fruchtbringende Gesellschaft</a>, the first society devoted to refining and standardising the German language, and he made Köthen a centre of learning and educational reform. His principality suffered heavily in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-i-prince-of-anhalt-kothen.jpg" alt="Louis I, Prince of Anhalt-Köthen" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ludwig_I._von_Anhalt-K%C3%B6then.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
